===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:thogh|tree=1}}
From {{ncog|enm|though}}, {{m|enm|thogh}}, from {{der|en|non|*þóh}} (later {{m|non|þó}}). Superseded (in most dialects) {{inh|en|enm|thegh}}, from {{inh|en|ang|þēah||though, although, even if, that, however, nevertheless, yet, still; whether}}. Both the Old Norse and Old English are from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*þauh||though}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*to-}}, suffixed with {{der|en|gem-pro|*-hw}} &lt; {{der|en|ine-pro|*-kʷe||and}}.

Akin to {{cog|sco|tho||though}}, {{cog|stq|dach||though}}, {{cog|fy|dôch}}, {{m|fy|dochs||though}}, {{cog|nl|doch||though}}, {{cog|de|doch||though}}, {{cog|da|dog||though, however}}, {{cog|sv|dock||however, still}}, {{cog|is|þó||though}}. More at [[that]].

